From 52e1de57b7edc210cb859474e43a52bd582198d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommaso Labieni <tommaso.labieni@entner-electronics.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 14:25:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] fix: raise POWERUP_MAX_RETRY from 0 to 3 for WiFi probe

bcmdhd's dummy_sdmmc_driver waits for BCM43456 to appear on the
SDIO bus via a semaphore. With POWERUP_MAX_RETRY=0 there is only
one 2-second attempt: it times out at ~4.9s and unregisters the
listener. mmc2 (SDIO host) then initializes at 5.067s with nothing
waiting for BCM43456.

With 3 retries the second attempt re-registers the dummy driver at
~4.917s. mmc2 finds BCM43456 at ~5.3s, dummy_probe fires and signals
the semaphore while dhd is still within its 2s window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile
index 461f4a4e1c46..44e44c972299 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ DHDCFLAGS = -Wall -Wstrict-prototypes -Wno-date-time -Wno-strict-prototypes   \
 	-DKEEP_ALIVE -DPKT_FILTER_SUPPORT -DDHDTCPACK_SUPPRESS                \
 	-DDHD_DONOT_FORWARD_BCMEVENT_AS_NETWORK_PKT -DOEM_ANDROID             \
 	-DMULTIPLE_SUPPLICANT -DTSQ_MULTIPLIER -DMFP -DDHD_8021X_DUMP         \
-	-DPOWERUP_MAX_RETRY=0 -DIFACE_HANG_FORCE_DEV_CLOSE -DWAIT_DEQUEUE     \
+	-DPOWERUP_MAX_RETRY=3 -DIFACE_HANG_FORCE_DEV_CLOSE -DWAIT_DEQUEUE     \
 	-DUSE_NEW_RSPEC_DEFS                                                  \
 	-DWL_EXT_IAPSTA -DWL_ESCAN -DCCODE_LIST -DSUSPEND_EVENT               \
 	-DKEY_INSTALL_CHECK                                                   \
